# MySQL row decoding uses the locked static parser

The mysql2 result decoder generated anonymous TextRow classes through
generate-function/index.js. A real synthetic-v1 MySQL semantics slice
completed all 50 selected operations, but executed-source qualification
rejected 18 anonymous generated sources from that producer. The capture
supervisor stopped the owned server gracefully and retained the failure.

Use mysql2 3.24.6's existing disableEval connection option in the product
driver and the harness's external-server connection. It selects the locked
static_text_parser/static_binary_parser modules, preserving the existing
dateStrings, supportBigNumbers and character-set settings. This choice
applies to the served driver as well as the graded adapter. It neither
relaxes source qualification nor changes package versions.

Verification compares the exact same operation IDs and decoded answers
against the prior real slice, then requires the unchanged source-binding
validator to accept each new TypeScript shard. Keep the rejected capture
as the negative control. Full lane grading remains separate from this
source-qualification check.
